(1. The Core Philosophy of Clean Architecture) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 600 Td
(Clean Architecture organizes software systems so that business logic remains completely independent) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 584 Td
(of frameworks, UI libraries, databases, and external I/O protocols. Key rules include:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 568 Td
(" The Dependency Rule: Source code dependencies must only point inwards toward high-level policies.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 552 Td
(" Entities: Business rules that encapsulate enterprise-wide critical business operations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 536 Td
(" Use Cases: Application-specific rules that orchestrate data flow between entities and interfaces.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
0.15 0.2 0.35 rg
50 506 Td
(2. SOLID Design Principles in Practice) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 486 Td
(Uncle Bob formalized 5 foundational object-oriented design principles:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 470 Td
(" Single Responsibility Principle \(SRP\): A class or module should have only one reason to change.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 454 Td
(" Open/Closed Principle \(OCP\): Software artifacts should be open for extension, closed for modification.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 438 Td
(" Liskov Substitution Principle \(LSP\): Subtypes must be substitutable for their base types.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 422 Td
(" Interface Segregation Principle \(ISP\): Clients should never be forced to depend on unused methods.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 406 Td
(" Dependency Inversion Principle \(DIP\): High-level modules must not depend on low-level details.) Tj
ET
